    "notes": [
      {
        "category": "summary",
        "text": "Security update for putty",
        "title": "Title of the patch"
      },
      {
        "category": "description",
        "text": "This update for putty fixes the following issues:\n\nChanges in putty:\n\n- Update to release 0.85\n\n  * Fixed a remotely triggerable use-after-free in Pageant.\n  * Fixed a remotely triggerable buffer overflow if the OpenSSH\n    encrypt-then-MAC cipher modes are in use. (Only used if a\n    server supports nothing else.)\n  * Fixed a buffer overflow in private key decryption, if the\n    private key is constructed maliciously. (Only triggerable on\n    purpose if you let somebody else generate a key for you.)\n  * Denial-of-service security fixes for where a server could\n    trigger a tight loop in PuTTY, and even a MITM can make it\n    consume unlimited memory at startup.\n\n- Fixed double free in RSA KEX error handling path can be triggered if the key sent by the server is unexpectedly short  [boo#1266375, CVE-2026-48850]\n- Fixed assertion failure in ECDSA signature verification can be triggered during initial key exchange via a crafted host key and signature  [boo#1266373, CVE-2026-48852]\n- Fixed TELNET session data is marked with trust sigils after authenticating to a proxy and allows for password prompt spoofing  [boo#1266374, CVE-2026-48851]\n",
        "title": "Description of the patch"
      },
      {
        "category": "details",
        "text": "openSUSE-Leap-16.0-packagehub-677",
        "title": "Patchnames"
      },
